****************************************************************************************
                                            
                                     smog_adjustPDB
                                            
    smog_adjustPDB is part of the SMOG 2 distribution, available at smog-server.org
                                            
   This tool will renumber the atoms in each chain, and modify the names of terminal
       residues, so that they are compatible with the definitions used by SMOG 2
                                            
                       See the SMOG manual for usage guidelines.
                                            
           For questions regarding this script, contact info@smog-server.org
****************************************************************************************

Will reformat the PDB file: /work/3PRG-clean.pdb

Will use the default map file for list of residue names.
New file will be written: /work/3PRG-adjusted.pdb

Mapping file "/opt/smog2/share/mapfiles/sbmMapExact" will be read.

Will use an exact-matching map file

NOTE 1: In mapping file, only astrisks found in atom names.  Since it is possible to use the ' or * convention, smog_adjustPDB will also interpret every ' in the PDB as a *.  Use "-noautorename" to disable this behavior.

Renamed residues/atoms in chain index 1: TYR-271->TYRT-271 


THERE WAS 1 NOTE. Even if you know what you are doing, it is always worth checking any notes.


	Adjustment of PDB is complete.

